# Milestone: M3
# Covers: forked runners sharing environment via '&'; both branches read and
#         write the outer var; join waits for both branches to complete.
# defer-to: M5 (chk runner needs urbi_step driver path for '&' separator)
#
# Reason:
#   '&' (OP_FORK_JOIN / OP_JOIN_WAIT) requires the realm-managed scheduler
#   path to actually schedule two strands and collect them.  The chk runner
#   uses the urbi_vm_run REPL path (realm == NULL); OP_FORK_JOIN produces a
#   TypeError in that context (see tests/chk/separator/comma_amp_unsupported.chk).
#   Cross-strand read/write ordering needs urbi_step driver to verify.
#
# Original urbiscript (activate at M5 with urbi_step chk driver):
# # check that forked runners can read environment
# # { var x = 0; { x.print() } & { x.print() }; x.print() };
# # [00000001] 0
# # [00000002] 0
# # [00000003] 0
# #
# # check that forked runners can write environment
# # { var x = 0; var y = 0; { x = 42 } & { y = 51 }; x.print(); y.print() };
# # [00000004] 42
# # [00000005] 51
